 <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What is the best robo-advisor for beginners?</h3><p>The best beginner robo-advisor has a low fee (~0.25%), a low or no minimum, automatic rebalancing, and easy goal setup. Match it to whether you want a taxable account, an IRA, or access to a human advisor.</p><h3>Are robo-advisors good for beginners?</h3><p>Yes — they handle diversification, rebalancing, and often tax-loss harvesting automatically, so beginners can invest sensibly without picking individual funds.</p><h3>How much do robo-advisors cost?</h3><p>Most charge about 0.25% of assets per year, plus the underlying fund fees. That's far cheaper than a traditional human advisor (~1%).</p><h3>How much do I need to start with a robo-advisor?</h3><p>Many have low or no minimums, so you can start with a small amount and add regularly. Consistent contributions matter more than the starting sum.</p><h3>Can you lose money with a robo-advisor?</h3><p>Yes — robo-advisors invest in market funds, so your balance rises and falls with the market. They manage allocation and risk level, not the risk of loss itself.</p><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@graph": [{"@type": "BlogPosting", "headline": "Best Robo-Advisor for Beginners (2026 Guide)", "about": "best robo-advisor for beginners", "url": "https://learners-link.blogspot.com/2026/08/best-robo-advisor-for-beginners-2026.html", "dateModified": "2026-09-15", "author": {"@type": "Organization", "name": "Learner's Link"}, "publisher": {"@type": "Organization", "name": "Learner's Link"}}, {"@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the best robo-advisor for beginners?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The best beginner robo-advisor has a low fee (~0.25%), a low or no minimum, automatic rebalancing, and easy goal setup. Match it to whether you want a taxable account, an IRA, or access to a human advisor."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Are robo-advisor